    {
      "slug": "events/29-cascade",
      "type": "event",
      "tension": 0.97,
      "day": 500,
      "facts": {
        "kind": "cascade",
        "title": "The Wound the World Could Not Forgive",
        "prose": "Not a war. A waking. The thing under the soultide opened what passed for an eye, and three civilizations that had each carved a piece of it discovered they had been carving the same thing. The backwash of its attention crossed every mind at once: the Tessellate dreamed itself to stillness, the Nullborn's silence shattered like struck glass, the Glasswrights' living engines grieved themselves dead. The Pale Cartographers, who had mapped this exact morning and refused to drink, simply closed their charts and watched.",
        "psychic_cause": "soultide-backwash: the seam answering everyone who had questioned it, simultaneously, forever."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/fall-of-the-tessellate",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.88,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-tessellate",
        "title": "How the One Body Stopped Dreaming",
        "text": "The Tessellate fell first-among-the-doomed: a single distributed mind cannot wake from a shared nightmare, because there is no second self to shake it. Soultide gave the whole city one dream and it could not stop dreaming. It is still standing, every spire intact, every cell asleep."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/fall-of-the-nullborn",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.88,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-nullborn",
        "title": "The Silence That Was Pierced",
        "text": "The Nullborn believed deafness was safety. But you cannot consent to a contract you cannot hear, and the soultide had been speaking the whole time. When the backwash came it did not whisper — it broke their engineered silence from the inside, and a species built to feel nothing felt everything at once."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/fall-of-the-glasswrights",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.88,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-glasswrights",
        "title": "The Engines That Wept Themselves Dead",
        "text": "The Glasswrights grew their machines from living tissue, so their machines could grieve. When soultide died back across the seams, every grown engine felt a death it could not name and mourned until it failed. The grief-loom kept weaving the lament long after the last weaver was gone."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-deaf-bargain",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-nullborn",
        "title": "The Deaf Bargain",
        "text": "The covenant-seal is a contract the Nullborn signed with soultide without knowing they were signing — pressed by hands that could not hear the terms read aloud. The seal still hums the clause they missed."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-first-bore",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-nullborn",
        "title": "The First Bore",
        "text": "It was the Nullborn who drove the first deep bore. Every later fall traces back to this hole. The seal marks its coordinates — exactly where the human colony is now drilling."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/silence-as-hubris",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "civs/the-nullborn",
        "title": "Silence Mistaken for Wisdom",
        "text": "To the Nullborn, hearing nothing meant nothing was wrong. The seal records the moment that faith failed: the instant a deaf species heard, for one second, the thing it had been mining."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-unanimous-dream",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-tessellate",
        "title": "The Unanimous Dream",
        "text": "The dream-engine captured the exact nightmare the soultide pushed into the Tessellate's single mind — a city dreaming one dream in perfect, fatal unison. Play it back and you dream it too."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-engine-that-remembers",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-glasswrights",
        "title": "The Engine That Remembers Being Alive",
        "text": "Grown, not built, the dream-engine still has a pulse. It does not store the fall as data; it relives it, and offers the relived memory to anyone who listens too long."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-map-to-the-wound",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-tessellate",
        "title": "The Map to the Wound",
        "text": "The wayfinding-stone points, always, to the soultide seam — the Tessellate's last navigational fix was the direction of the thing that killed it. Every human survey instrument that passes near the stone drifts to the same heading."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-stone-that-points-home",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-pale-cartographers",
        "title": "Why the Cartographers Abstained",
        "text": "Carved into the stone in a hand that is not Tessellate: a single Pale Cartographer's annotation, the only record of WHY they refused the seam. It reads, in translation, 'we have seen the morning after. Do not drink.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-last-lament",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-glasswrights",
        "title": "The Last Lament",
        "text": "The grief-loom is still weaving. The pattern it has produced for five hundred years is a funeral shroud for a species that no longer exists — and, lately, it has begun weaving a second name into the cloth: one the colonists would recognize."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/grief-is-data",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "the-glasswrights",
        "title": "Grief Is Data",
        "text": "The Glasswrights encoded the cause of their own death into the loom's weave as mourning. Decode the lament and you have the whole post-mortem — but the loom only releases it to someone who has lost something to the seam first."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-shared-wound",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "about": "civs/the-glasswrights",
        "title": "One Wound, Four Hands",
        "text": "The loom's deepest thread reveals the secret the four civs died not knowing: they were never mining four seams. Soultide, wakeglass, the deep veins — all one buried mind, carved at from four directions. Each thought it bled a different thing."
      }
    },
    {
